<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <link rel="icon" href="images/sherman-logo-title.png" type="image/icon type">
    <title>About</title>

    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">

    <script>
      try {
        var savedTheme = localStorage.getItem('sherman-theme');
        if (savedTheme) {
          document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', savedTheme);
        }
      } catch (e) {}
    </script>

    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Anton&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Fraunces:ital@1&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="stylesheets/shared/general.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="stylesheets/shared/sherman-header.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="stylesheets/pages/about.css">
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="main">
      <div class="about-eyebrow">[ about ]</div>

      <h1 class="about-title">about</h1>

      <p class="about-text">
        Sherman is a small, strange shop for things that don't need to
        exist, built anyway. Every product gets the same care whether
        it's useful or not - that's the whole point.
      </p>

      <a class="about-link link-primary" href="https://sanjuontheweb.github.io/The-Portfolio/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        visit the site
      </a>

      <a href="sherman" class="back-to-shop">&larr; sherman</a>
    </div>

    <script type = "module" src = "javascripts/auth-guard.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
